FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/banner.rs:131 — `terminal_width()` returns unbounded `COLUMNS` and `print_banner` does `" ".repeat(pad)` per row with no cap, so `COLUMNS=999999999` allocates ~500MB per row / ~2.5GB total and OOMs the session at startup from env alone — unbounded allocation with no memory bound — cap the width actually used for centering (e.g. `terminal_width().min(200)` or clamp `pad` to a small constant).
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:506 — `!!` dispatch does not account for `in_multiline`, so `!!` at a `..  N` prompt re-executes the last typed line through `execute_line` and duplicates it into `multiline_buffer` instead of repeating a complete line; the resulting block has different source than what was typed and no test drives `session_loop` with opener then `!!` — add an explicit rule (refuse `!!` while `in_multiline`, or define buffer-aware repeat) and a test that would settle it: opener, `!!`, close, assert buffer contents.
3. [MINOR] src/repl/mod.rs:635 — `:history` prints `entry` raw, so `:prompt rb> ` and `:prompt rb>` (which render different prompts and repeat differently) are visually identical and a saved file carries invisible trailing whitespace — make the distinction observable (e.g. visibly mark trailing space in `:history`) or store display and repeat forms separately.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 3
